Underbrim started from Boring Notch v2.8-rc.1 (commit fb26431, 25 September
2026). This repository keeps Boring Notch's history: the commits up to
fb26431 are the Boring Notch authors' own, and Underbrim's changes come after
it.

Changes from Boring Notch (GPL-3.0, section 5(a)), made in October 2026:

  - A separate app: its own name, icon, identity and settings, and no
    updater. Boring Notch's names in the project are replaced with
    Underbrim's. A file header's project line names the project, not the
    author; the authors' "Created by" lines are kept.
  - The open notch drawn as one shape growing from the hardware notch, with
    every tab one low row, a pin that keeps it open, a second activity in a
    bubble beside it, keyboard access and Reduce Motion alternatives.
  - Home widgets you choose, order and size: Now Playing, Calendar, Mirror,
    Quick Launch, Timer, Shortcuts, Scratchpad, System, Reminders, Unread,
    Calls and Prayer, any of which can be pinned beside the camera.
  - Coding agents in the notch: Claude Code and Codex sessions read from the
    files those tools keep, Qwen Code, Qoder, Cursor and Antigravity through
    hooks, plan usage and token counts, approvals and questions answered in
    the notch through optional hooks, and a creature with sounds for each
    agent.
  - A Sound page with a volume for each app.
  - Clipboard history encrypted on the Mac, screenshots on the Shelf,
    download progress from Chrome and Safari, a meeting countdown, and
    battery and headphone details.
  - The iPhone's Live Activities, deliveries, calls, Focus, Caps Lock and
    unlocking shown in the notch.
  - Prayer times, worked out on the Mac.
  - Volume and brightness shown in the notch, Settings with its own look and
    a search for every setting, and a welcome tour inside the notch.
  - Twelve languages, with Arabic laid out right to left.
  - On the lock screen, only Home and the widgets that show nothing private;
    many fixes to hover, clicks, drags, the Shelf and the camera.

